1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,190
This car jumps without a ramp.

2
00:00:02,270 --> 00:00:04,050
Its suspension launches it.

3
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:07,650
But the moment those tires leave
the road, they lose their grip.

4
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:11,150
So what does making a
supercar jump actually prove?

5
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:14,300
This is BYD's Yangwang U9.

6
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:18,840
Ordinary springs store and release
energy, while dampers control the motion.

7
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:21,000
This car adds active control:

8
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:24,660
powered actuators can apply force
between the wheels and body.

9
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:27,709
During the launch, the tires
push against the pavement,

10
00:00:27,719 --> 00:00:29,340
and the pavement pushes back.

11
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:32,680
That upward force accelerates
the car before takeoff.

12
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:35,880
Once the wheels lift clear,
the ground stops pushing.

13
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:39,200
Momentum carries the car
upward while gravity slows it,

14
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:40,640
then brings it back down.

15
00:00:41,390 --> 00:00:43,810
Now put that same car into a corner.

16
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:48,330
The body tends to lean outward, loading
the suspension differently on each side.

17
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:51,030
For the jump, the system lifts the car.

18
00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:55,430
Here, it adjusts forces across the
suspension to oppose that lean.

19
00:00:55,730 --> 00:00:57,570
Same ability to apply force.

20
00:00:57,710 --> 00:00:58,710
Different job.

21
00:00:58,990 --> 00:01:01,010
This is active body control.

22
00:01:01,290 --> 00:01:03,290
The point isn't to make the car float.

23
00:01:03,390 --> 00:01:06,910
It's to manage how the body moves
while the tires deal with the road.

24
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:10,630
A flatter body, though, doesn't
automatically mean more grip.

25
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:13,950
Brake hard, and the body
tends to pitch forward.

26
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:16,550
Active suspension can oppose that dive.

27
00:01:16,790 --> 00:01:18,100
Hit an uneven patch,

28
00:01:18,110 --> 00:01:22,210
and the wheels need room to move without
making the cabin copy every movement.

29
00:01:22,450 --> 00:01:26,630
That's a balancing act between body
control, tire contact, and comfort.

30
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:29,470
The system still has
limited travel and force.

31
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:32,710
It can't turn a rough road
into a perfectly smooth one.

32
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:35,950
And a level car doesn't
make the corner disappear.

33
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:39,390
Your body still needs a sideways
force to follow the turn.

34
00:01:39,550 --> 00:01:40,910
The seat provides it.

35
00:01:41,050 --> 00:01:44,810
You still feel pressed into the
bolster, even when the car leans less.

36
00:01:45,150 --> 00:01:47,590
Body control isn't force cancellation.

37
00:01:48,290 --> 00:01:49,550
Watch the jump again.

38
00:01:49,770 --> 00:01:52,850
The suspension builds the launch
while the tires are grounded.

39
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:56,410
Then contact breaks, and
gravity takes over the flight.

40
00:01:56,790 --> 00:01:59,910
That hop is the spectacular
part of the demonstration.

41
00:02:00,130 --> 00:02:03,430
The useful engineering is controlling
body movement when you brake,

42
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:05,570
turn, and hit uneven pavement.

43
00:02:05,890 --> 00:02:07,350
A supercar can jump.

44
00:02:07,590 --> 00:02:10,630
Most of the time, its suspension
has a much harder job:

45
00:02:10,850 --> 00:02:12,710
keeping it composed on the ground.
